<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      The music frame on wave 02 stops being a square and becomes a PORTRAIT: the cover's square
      across the full width plus a text band under it (DESIGN §10.2, the owner's decision).

      The square tile (0570) assumed the text lies ON TOP of the cover: then the frame
      and the picture coincide. In fact they coincided only approximately: 7x9 tracks are
      259.9x264.7px, and the square cover fitted in whole (`contain`) left five-pixel
      bands at the edges. The bands were exactly what the frame must avoid: it shows
      a picture, not a picture framed in its own background.

      The new composition removes the question by construction: the cover layer is the square itself, pinned to
      the top of the frame across its whole width, so "the frame's width" and "the picture's width" are the same
      number for any grid geometry. The frame needs height for the square plus a text band:

        width(7)   = 33.7*7 + 4*6    = 259.9
        height(10) = 25.86*10 + 4*9  = 294.6   ⇒ 34.7px remain under the square

      Eleven rows (324.5) would give the text its whole height, but the frame then
      stretched noticeably taller than its neighbours: the owner looked at both and chose ten. The band
      under the square is narrower than two lines of text, and they overlap the picture's bottom: the cloud
      is there for that (see wave-02.css): the text reads on it, and the picture is not cropped.

      The row is taken from "Today" (14→13). The dominant tile loses ~26px of height; the trail map does not
      notice (its content is centred), and the air spacer between tiles stays:
      "Today" ends on row 17, the frame starts at 19, row 18 is empty.

      Considered and rejected: keep the grid and NARROW the card to 199px so the square with
      the text fits the old 264.7. The frame's width then does not depend on the grid, but the cover
      loses a quarter of its side, and the whole wave is built on the picture being seen as
      large as possible.
    -->
    <changeSet id="0580-wave-02-music-portrait" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"col": 19, "row": 19, "colSpan": 7, "rowSpan": 10}$J$::jsonb),
        '{tiles,today}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 5, "colSpan": 13, "rowSpan": 13}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"col": 19, "row": 20, "colSpan": 7, "rowSpan": 9}$J$::jsonb),
        '{tiles,today}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 5, "colSpan": 13, "rowSpan": 14}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
